===Etymology 1===
{{affix|en|clean|-er|id2=agent noun|gloss2=[[agent noun]]}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A person whose occupation is to clean floors, windows and other things.
# A device that [[clean]]s, such as the [[vacuum cleaner]].
# A [[substance]] used for [[cleaning]], a cleaning agent.
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} A professional [[laundry]] or [[dry cleaner]] {{gloss|business}}.  {{gloss|This form is now interpreted as plural and usually spelled without an apostrophe, even in official usage, to justify the removal of the apostrophe. It was traditionally spelled ''[[cleaner's]]'' with an apostrophe because this is grammatically correct, as can be seen with forms such as ''go to the [[doctor's]]'', which cannot be reinterpreted as plural.}}
#: ''I'll have to take this shirt to the '''cleaners'''.''
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[hitman]]; a hired [[assassin]], usually in the employ of an organized crime syndicate, such as the [[mafia]].

